# Decompiled game code — derived from the local Steam install, never distribute
decomp/

# Build output
bin/
obj/
*.user

# Packaged releases. Built by scripts\package.ps1 and attached to a release rather
# than tracked, so the repository never carries a stale zip claiming to be current.
dist/

# The NVDA controller client. Deliberately shipped to players and deliberately not
# committed: it is LGPL 2.1 third-party binary, so it rides in the release assets
# where its licence text travels with it. See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
# scripts\package.ps1 says where to put it if a fresh clone does not have it.
lib/x64/

# Scratch
*.log

# Workspace material, not part of the mod. README, CHANGELOG, LICENSE and
# THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES are what a user needs — what it does, what changed, and what it is
# built on. The rest is how the work gets done: a running status log, the game research
# behind it, and post-mortems of our own mistakes. None of that is a user's business, and
# none of it is referenced from the files that do ship.
project_status.md
docs/

# AI assistant instruction and context files. Kept out of the repository so the
# published project reads as the project rather than as a workspace. PRINCIPLES.md
# belongs here despite reading like documentation: it is written to steer how the
# next session works, not to describe the mod to a user.
PRINCIPLES.md
CLAUDE.md
AGENTS.md
GEMINI.md
.cursorrules
.windsurfrules
rules/
rules.md
.claude/
.cursor/
.aider*
